issues=[]
def issue(id,kind,priority,title,where,evidence,impact,fix,test,confidence):
 issues.append(dict(id=id,kind=kind,priority=priority,title=title,where=where,evidence=evidence,impact=impact,fix=fix,test=test,confidence=confidence))
issue('01','Bug','High','CanvasKit failure after an action already committed','S3 W16 · Training and Quick Match',
 'Two CanvasKit Aborted() errors occurred. Finn’s technique gain remained. The Quick Match result also advanced the career to Week 17. Reloading recovered the saved progress.',
 'The player cannot safely infer whether to retry. A successful mutation followed by a failed presentation is a serious trust problem.',
 'Fix the rendering failure and make the recovery screen report whether the action committed. Show the saved week and completed action.',
 'Run a long web session across drills and Quick Matches. Force a presentation failure after settlement. Verify one spend, one result, and an honest recovery message.',
 'Observed; rendering root cause not isolated. No lasting save loss was found.')
issue('02','Investigate','High','The built-in browser renderer crashed in a long session','S5 W10 · After a request interaction',
 'The browser showed its crash page. Reloading that tab was blocked by the browser tool’s data-URL policy. A new tab recovered the same Week 10 save. The pending refusal had not committed.',
 'This interrupted the run and made normal recovery unavailable in this browser surface.',
 'Investigate memory and graphics pressure in long sessions. Preserve a clear reopen-and-resume path. Track app failures separately from browser-tool failures.',
 'Repeat long sessions in the built-in browser and a normal browser. Compare renderer memory and crash logs. Test iOS separately.',
 'Crash observed; an app memory leak or iOS crash is not proven.')
issue('03','Bug','High','Automatic lineup repair put players in the wrong roles','S4 W8 and S5 W5 · Team sheet',
 'After a hero-license change, Ollie Moss, a forward, appeared in defense. Later, Sol, a midfielder, occupied a defensive slot while Finn Ash was available on the bench. Both were corrected before kickoff.',
 'A management action can silently weaken the team. A player may blame tactics or balance for a lineup repair error.',
 'Repair lineups by natural role, availability, promises, and license status. Preview substitutions before confirming a license handoff.',
 'Repeat these transitions with same-role cover. Assert a valid 11-player lineup, then inspect the rendered team sheet after each change.',
 'Repeated in the live run. The matches used the manually corrected lineups.')
issue('04','Investigate','Medium','Presentation transitions sometimes swallowed the next click','Throughout · Training, signings, requests, navigation',
 'Closing a drill or selecting a new screen immediately after a presentation sometimes did nothing. A fresh read and a later click worked. Stat gains and TP spending were not duplicated in the checked cases.',
 'The flow feels unresponsive. Rapid automation also makes this easier to encounter than ordinary play.',
 'Show when a presentation owns input. Make the first close action deterministic. Avoid a hidden overlay intercepting a different control.',
 'Test fast human-like taps, keyboard activation, and Reduce Motion. Separate a correct skip action from a dropped navigation action.',
 'Observed under fast automation; normal human frequency is not measured.')
issue('05','Bug','Medium','The squad register contains nested buttons on web','S1 W5 · Squad register',
 'React reported a player-name button inside a summary-row button and warned about invalid button nesting and possible hydration trouble.',
 'This can confuse keyboard focus and assistive technology. The warning did not itself crash the game in this run.',
 'Use one actionable row, or separate sibling controls. Preserve a clear accessible name for summary and training actions.',
 'Inspect the rendered DOM and keyboard focus order. Confirm that no button is a descendant of another button.',
 'Console warning observed; no hydration failure was demonstrated.')
issue('06','Bug','Medium','Contract radios expose selection with the wrong state','Contract talks · Term and promise choices',
 'A radio click changed the contract choice, but the automation could not read it as checked. MarketScreen.tsx uses accessibilityRole="radio" with accessibilityState.selected on the inspected term control.',
 'A selected radio may not be announced correctly. This is an accessibility defect, not evidence that the contract failed.',
 'Use the checked state for radio choices. Audit the sibling contract radio groups and their group labels.',
 'Choose each term with keyboard and a screen reader. Verify exactly one checked option and the submitted contract value.',
 'Live symptom plus source confirmation. Clicking was a reliable workaround.')
issue('07','Bug','Low','The license footer promises AUTO behavior in MANUAL mode','S1 W4 · Prematch footer',
 'The footer said licensed heroes fire automatically while MANUAL was selected. The shared English footer still makes that unconditional claim.',
 'A new player can misunderstand which controls they must use.',
 'Make the footer follow the current power mode. Explain separately that Quick Match always uses automatic powers.',
 'Read the team sheet in MANUAL and AUTO, then compare it with Quick Match behavior.',
 'Observed and source-confirmed copy mismatch.')
issue('08','Bug','Low','Assistant-coach dismissal calls the assistant the head coach','S5 W1 · Dismiss Hana',
 'The cancel control’s accessible name said to keep Hana as head coach. CoachStaffOverlay uses the head-coach label for both roles.',
 'The spoken action describes the wrong staff position.',
 'Include the actual coach role in the accessible label, matching the visible dismissal context.',
 'Inspect both head-coach and assistant-coach dismissal dialogs with accessibility output.',
 'Observed accessible-name bug; source confirmed. The visible generic cancel copy is a separate surface.')
issue('09','Investigate','Medium','A pre-listing “Best bid” did not match the bids received','S1 W17 · Sell Ed Stone',
 'The preview showed $27,471. The best actual offer after listing was $25,413. That is $2,058 less, about 7.5%. The sale completed at the actual offer.',
 'The difference can break a tight transfer or construction budget.',
 'If the first number is an estimate, label it as an estimate. Otherwise freeze the quoted offer or explain what changed.',
 'Compare the same player’s pre-listing estimate and generated offers without advancing the week.',
 'Mismatch observed once. The intended quote contract still needs review.')
issue('10','Clarity','Medium','Cup history omitted the play-in round','S1 W19 · Hero Cup history',
 'The cup screen showed later rounds but omitted the play-in. After an interrupted elimination flow, the exact final score could not be recovered there.',
 'A player cannot reconstruct their own cup run or revisit an early elimination.',
 'Include every played round, including play-ins, with opponent, score, and result status.',
 'Lose a play-in, revisit the cup screen, and confirm the result remains available after reload.',
 'Observed. The final score of this particular S1 tie remains unverified; it was 0–1 at 85 minutes.')
issue('11','Bug','Low','The opening pitch tutorial returned after a mid-career fire','S2 W18 · Home inbox',
 'After the Training Pitch was destroyed, the startup prompt returned and referred to the initial budget still including $8,000.',
 'The text describes a new club rather than the current recovery problem.',
 'Use a recovery-specific prompt when an established club loses a facility. Keep onboarding completion separate from facility existence.',
 'Destroy the pitch in a later season and inspect the inbox, budget wording, and rebuild action.',
 'Observed after the fire.')
issue('12','Clarity','Low','A heavy defeat triggered an implausibly upbeat coach line','S3 W14 · Ulric 12–0 Bramble',
 'The full-time report said “We belonged out there. Remember that bit.” after a 12–0 defeat. The archived live report confirms both the score and line.',
 'The coach sounds detached from the match. It weakens the otherwise strong character writing.',
 'Gate reaction lines by score margin and context. Keep humor, but distinguish encouragement from denying the result.',
 'Review blowout losses, narrow losses, and giant-killing wins against the eligible reaction pools.',
 'Observed copy/context mismatch; this is an editorial judgment, not a simulation bug.')
issue('13','Investigate','Low','Rival presentation and reported hero count did not agree','S6 W12 · Ashford introduction and team sheet',
 'Bruce Wain received a Shadow Mark rival introduction. The following Ashford docket reported zero rival heroes.',
 'It is unclear whether the introduction describes a manager, a squad hero, or an active opponent threat.',
 'Clarify what the count measures. If it means active opposition heroes, make the introduction and lineup evidence consistent.',
 'Trace that exact fixture from introduction through opponent roster and active powers. Check other named rival fixtures.',
 'Visible mismatch; the correct underlying roster count was not established.')
issue('14','Clarity','Medium','My first scouting trip was started too late','S1 W17 and later scouting windows',
 'The first attempted S1 mission returned after the signing window and was correctly warned against. Later, 3- and 4-week mission previews required careful selection. I did not prove that scouting was unavailable at its intended Week 15 reveal.',
 'Missing one dispatch opportunity can delay an upgrade by a season. My own missed timing contributed.',
 'Show a last useful dispatch date and a persistent report-arrival reminder. Explain why adding a role filter changes travel time.',
 'Run a first-time-player test around Weeks 13–18. Record discovery and dispatch timing without coaching the player.',
 'Observed usability cost plus agent error; not a proven unlock bug.')
issue('15','Clarity','High','The fire choice hides the exact building at risk and uses cheerful framing','S2 W18 · The Firebreak Decision',
 'The risky preview said “70%: Lose the top Fan Shop or largest facility.” The pitch was lost. The safe choice guaranteed losing two small facilities, yet used generic “Smaller reward” wording. Source confirms the risky branch is 30% save-all, 70% lose-primary.',
 'This is a severe club decision without an exact affected-building preview. The lost pitch cut weekly TP from 42 to 18.',
 'Name the buildings and their lost weekly output before selection. Use cost-and-risk language for destructive choices. Foreshadow the departure-linked retaliation.',
 'Preview each choice with several facility layouts. The named losses must equal the actual losses.',
 'Preview ambiguity and loss observed. This does NOT prove the wrong building was destroyed.')
issue('16','Balance','High','An awakening can make a usable player unavailable','S3 Ari and S5 Finn · Full license capacity',
 'Ari awakened without a free permit and stayed unlicensed. Finn’s S5 awakening created another license squeeze. Buying the fourth permit required $200,000; Ari was later sold to help fund it.',
 'A supposed reward can remove a player from the practical selection pool and force a sale or a weak replacement.',
 'Keep license choices meaningful, but preview the consequence. Consider allowing an unlicensed hero to play with the power disabled.',
 'Compare the current rule with a dormant-power option. Check Starter promises, ordinary-player value, and whether permit purchases still feel worthwhile.',
 'Observed rule consequence. Changing it is a design decision.')
issue('17','Clarity','High','Full permits silently block promised starters from awakening','S6 W11 · Fifth license',
 'The eligibility code excludes available players with Starter or Captaincy promises when no permit is free. Buying permit five for $300,000 was followed by Wes Tate’s awakening in the next match.',
 'The manager cannot plan hero growth from the visible promise and license descriptions alone.',
 'Show why the club currently has no eligible awakening candidates. State the permit interaction when offering a promise or license.',
 'Build a full-license XI of promised ordinary starters. Confirm that the UI explains the block, then update it after buying capacity.',
 'Rule verified in source. The immediate awakening supports the mechanism but does not prove a universal one-match guarantee.')
issue('18','Balance','Medium','Starter promises make tactical flexibility expensive','S4–S6 · Recruitment and formation selection',
 'Cheap multi-year Starter promises secured strong recruits. By D1, promised players occupied nearly every line of a natural 4–4–2. Changing formation often meant violating promises or using unsuitable roles.',
 'A negotiation benefit can reduce future tactical choices without a clear forward view.',
 'Preview formation restrictions at signing. Consider a meaningful renegotiation route or a starts-over-time promise rather than only an absolute lineup requirement.',
 'Track the number of valid natural-role formations before and after each promise. Test whether the warning changes signing decisions.',
 'Observed tradeoff, amplified by my promise-heavy strategy. Keep consequences for promises.')
issue('19','Balance','High','Academy recruitment allowed immediate resale profit','S2 W1 · Dara Lane',
 'Signed Dara for $500 and immediately sold her for $6,052. Profit was $5,552 without a training session or elapsed week.',
 'The intake becomes a cash coupon instead of a development decision.',
 'Close immediate resale arbitrage with a narrow registration, fee, or valuation rule. Keep cheap long-term academy recruitment.',
 'Compare immediate resale with one-season development. Confirm that genuine academy successes still earn a useful transfer fee.',
 'Executed exploit. Intake is limited, so this was bounded profit, not infinite money.')
issue('20','Balance','High','A legal scout outlier overwhelmed D5 recruitment value','S2 W4 · Jae Stone',
 'Jae arrived at OVR 86 for $20,852 and $258/week, with DEF 117 and PAS/STA 113/117. The earlier S1 league view put average D5 club strength near 46. These are different measures, but the role upgrade was enormous.',
 'One affordable discovery sharply reduced the need to improve ordinary starters.',
 'Review within-division value and strength distribution. Price extreme role specialists more carefully before imposing a blanket scouting nerf.',
 'Measure outcome and purchase-value distributions over scout seeds. Include wages, promises, and same-role incumbent improvement.',
 'Observed outlier. Source’s D5 scout ceiling is OVR 88, so Jae does not demonstrate a code violation of that ceiling.')
issue('21','Balance','High','Early cup mismatches became long, one-sided eliminations','S2–S4 · Round of 32',
 'Lost 0–13 to D2 Northgate in S2, 0–12 to D1 Ulric in S3, and 1–8 to D1 Rookwood in S4. S2 Northgate’s Cal Hart scored ten.',
 'The cup often offered little agency after the first successful round. A long watched rout delays the next useful management decision.',
 'Keep the possibility of a giant opponent. Improve the mismatch briefing, underdog rewards, and safe “finish match” option. Review margin and draw distributions.',
 'Measure upset rates, score margins, and time spent after likely elimination across division gaps.',
 'Repeated live outcomes. One career cannot establish the intended overall upset rate.')
issue('22','Balance','High','The last D1 stretch and entire final cup run lost suspense','S6 · Title run and five cup matches',
 'D1 was secured with three league games left. The cup run was 10–0, 10–0, 4–0, 8–0, 7–0: 39 scored, none conceded. This followed genuine early D1 difficulty.',
 'The finale delivered a satisfying reward but little competitive uncertainty.',
 'Test top-club resistance against developed squads. Improve authored top-end roster strengths and tactical variety before adding hidden catch-up scaling.',
 'Run several optimized and ordinary careers. Compare close-match rate, cup finalist strength, and goal concentration after entering D1.',
 'Strong signal in this run; not proof all careers or seeds finish this way.')
issue('23','Balance','Medium','Save Energy was a very strong default','Most watched matches · All divisions',
 'Source uses 0.60 energy drain and 0.90 movement for Save Energy, versus 1.65 drain and 1.12 movement for All Out. The carrier exception reduced the attacking cost. Saving energy worked in both narrow matches and routs.',
 'The energy decision may collapse into one opening choice and a late chase button.',
 'Test pressure, loose-ball, and transition costs before changing the multipliers. Give each mode a clear useful match context.',
 'Use identical teams and seeds to compare modes. Measure chances, possession recoveries, energy, and win rate, not score alone.',
 'Rule values verified. Superiority was not established by controlled A/B matches.')
issue('24','Clarity','Medium','Large raw stats did not mean equally large gains','Training and D1 squad planning',
 'I invested heavily in PAC before checking its shallow speed curve. Source notes speed at PAC 999 is 146.9 versus 116.9 at PAC 112. Meanwhile Sam reached REF 629 and the forwards reached SHO 404/395.',
 'The visible +stat reward can conceal very different marginal match value. Specialist growth also appears to outpace some opponents.',
 'Explain diminishing returns in useful terms. Show a simple role-relevant estimate or training guidance without turning the UI into a formula sheet.',
 'Check how each extra drill affects actual actions at low, medium, and high ratings. Verify caps and curves before tuning growth.',
 'Stats and pace curve verified. The relative match value of every attribute was not measured.')
issue('25','Clarity','Low','Correction: training already has a confirmed batch skip','Across six 30-week seasons',
 'I overlooked the outside-dismiss shortcut. The game already previews and confirms a batch, then runs its remaining drills when the presentation closes. Injury and stat-cap checks still apply.',
 'My original report overstated the repeated-animation problem. Selecting different players and drills is ordinary management; this run does not establish that it needs a shortcut.',
 'Keep the current training flow. A saved cross-player plan is an optional convenience proposal only, and has not been implemented.',
 'The existing TrainingDrillModal dismiss handler and batch tests verify completion of confirmed remaining drills. No reliable human click count was recorded.',
 'Corrected after the owner explained outside dismissal. I knew individual animations were skippable but had not accounted for the complete batch skip.')
issue('26','Balance','Medium','Training penalties encouraged postponing the training loop','S1 and S2 · Story results',
 'Bad story outcomes imposed 75% or 90% training periods. I banked TP through penalties, then ran large batches after they ended. The delayed batch was more attractive than ordinary weekly spending.',
 'The optimal response can be to stop engaging with the main growth loop for several weeks.',
 'Keep setbacks, but consider effects that create a new choice rather than a waiting period. Make duration and expiry unmissable.',
 'Compare immediate training and delayed training under each event. Look for safe options that dominate risky ones even on expected value.',
 'Executed timing strategy. Early missed gambles do not prove the RNG was unfair.')
issue('27','Balance','Medium','Some personal requests had almost no real cost','S2/S3/S6 · Individual training penalties',
 'Granting an individual drill penalty was cheap when I could train someone else. Eli’s S6 chef request reduced only his drills for three weeks; he was a reserve I was not developing.',
 'A personality event can become an automatic yes for reserves and an automatic no for squad-wide costs.',
 'Vary the relevant tradeoff by the player’s actual role and plans. Preserve a few easy kindness choices for warmth.',
 'Compare acceptance rates for core starters and unused reserves. Check whether the displayed downside ever changes a decision.',
 'Observed strategy; not every easy request needs a nerf.')
issue('28','Balance','Medium','Late money had less decision value than early money','Economy from S1 to S6',
 'S1 cash briefly fell to $296. Before the last S6 league settlement, cash was $1,463,398. Gates reached six figures. Green Bull was used twice in S4, then lost priority to targeted gains and recruits.',
 'The early budget creates tension; the late budget often becomes a score. Existing sinks were not exhausted in this run.',
 'Compare the value of existing upgrades and Green Bull before adding costs. Avoid flat wage inflation or random destruction as the first fix.',
 'Run a matched spending-policy comparison. Include overlooked recovery and facility upgrades, then measure whether each purchase changes a real decision.',
 'Cash growth observed. My unused late upgrades and cash mean “the economy has no sinks” is NOT established.')
issue('29','Pacing','Medium','Power presentations briefly displaced tactical controls','Watched matches · Compact browser HUD',
 'Power overlays replaced the coaching dock. In the S6 Silverbeck comeback, reading and clearing presentations delayed access to a shape change while the match kept advancing at 3×.',
 'The spectacle competes with live coaching, especially for rapid input or accessibility tools.',
 'Keep pause and core tactical controls reachable during power displays. Offer compact repeat presentations without adding more forced pauses.',
 'Test a tactical change during overlapping powers at 1× and 3×. Measure blocked-control time and accidental skip/navigation behavior.',
 'Observed UI structure. Automation latency amplified the missed timing.')
issue('30','Docs','Medium','The handoff and some canonical notes disagree with live rules','Guide used during this run',
 'The handoff warned against automatic later licensing, while Cal and Ed received free active slots. Old four-license assumptions failed: the live UI offered permits five and six. Its claim that higher drill tiers are always more TP-efficient also fails at T4 versus T5.',
 'A stale guide can produce bad play decisions and false bug reports.',
 'Separate intended rules, current implementation, and old findings. Generate simple cost and capacity reference tables from the same data as the UI.',
 'Reconcile license behavior, scout timing, drill economics, and speed unlocks against the current build.',
 'Documentation drift confirmed. Do not automatically treat an old guide as the correct behavior.')
