fix_status = {'01': ('Unresolved', 'The CanvasKit abort was observed, but its cause is not isolated. Existing recovery already warns that the last action may be saved. A new graphics or save-recovery change would be speculative. No decision needed; it needs crash diagnostics and a repeatable trigger.'), '02': ('Unresolved', 'The browser renderer crash and tool reload limit are distinct failures. No app leak or native crash was established. A browser-process crash cannot be repaired by screen copy. No design decision needed; long-session diagnostics remain.'), '03': ('Unresolved', 'Shared repair prefers the outgoing player’s natural role and uses an outfield fallback when necessary. Formation slots live outside that helper. The exact two recorded transitions lack enough before-state evidence to prove which path caused them. Existing lineup regression checks were run; no speculative automatic rearrangement was added.'), '04': ('Qualified', 'Fast automation amplified this finding. The training presentation has an intentional short tap guard, and outside dismissal completes a confirmed batch. A dropped normal user action is not yet reproduced. No input guard was removed.'), '05': ('Fixed locally', 'The player summary uses one InfoTip action. The training button remains a sibling. Live browser inspection found zero nested buttons, and the player file still opens.'), '06': ('Fixed locally', 'Term, promise, license handoff, and pitch-card radios now expose checked state. The live negotiation showed exactly the selected promise as checked and updated the offer text.'), '07': ('Fixed locally', 'The footer explains watched AUTO/MANUAL and Quick Match AUTO. Checked in the browser with MANUAL selected.'), '08': ('Fixed locally', 'The dismiss dialog uses the actual coach role in its accessible cancel label. All seven catalogs use the same parameterized key.'), '09': ('Fixed locally', 'An unlisted sale quote is an Estimated bid. A listed offer remains Best bid. The focused view-model check passes.'), '10': ('Fixed locally', 'The cup screen keeps the drawn play-in round card after the round ends. The main knockout bracket remains compact.'), '11': ('Fixed locally', 'A missing pitch after onboarding gets a rebuild message. It no longer claims the original budget still contains $8,000.'), '12': ('Fixed locally', 'Heavy losses use the heavy-loss coach pool, including cup mismatches. Narrow giant losses keep their encouragement.'), '13': ('Clarified locally', 'The team sheet now labels its hero count as the expected XI. A rival introduction can feature a hero elsewhere in the squad.'), '14': ('Corrected', 'This was mainly my timing error. The game already warns when a mission returns after the final signing window. I did not establish a late scouting unlock.'), '15': ('Clarity fixed; choice remains', 'The fire preview now names actual buildings, levels, and benefits at risk. Its alternative says No buildings lost. Generic choice copy no longer calls a guaranteed loss a reward. Choice: keep this severe story, or soften its loss/rebuild cost.'), '16': ('Your choice', 'Helpers explain why an unlicensed hero must stay on the bench. Choice: keep the current license rule, or let unlicensed heroes play with powers disabled.'), '17': ('Fixed locally', 'The permit office shows the season tally and names normal players blocked by starting promises. Contract talks explain the permit requirement. The warning clears when a license is freed. SUPER is explicitly described as a drill bonus chance.'), '18': ('Your choice', 'Starter and Captain promises can prevent a formation or lineup change. Choice: keep a guaranteed place in every legal XI, or use a starts quota or a renegotiation option.'), '19': ('Your choice', 'A $500 academy signing was sold immediately for $6,052. Choice: keep trading profit as a reward, or restrict immediate resale with a wait or fee.'), '20': ('Your choice; measure before tuning', 'The D5 scout found a legal OVR 86 bargain. Choice: keep rare major upgrades, or narrow their strength or raise their price. This one result does not justify a blanket scout nerf.'), '21': ('Your choice', 'Early cup draws produced extreme defeats. Choice: keep the open all-division draw, or protect early rounds with closer seeding.'), '22': ('Your choice; measure before tuning', 'The last cup run was 39–0 after an optimized career. Choice: keep a victory lap after building a dominant club, or aim for stronger final opposition.'), '23': ('Unproven balance claim', 'Save Energy worked well in this route. A same-team, same-seed comparison across all effort modes was not performed. No nerf is justified yet; no decision is required from this evidence.'), '24': ('Clarity fixed locally', 'The PAC tooltip now says doubling PAC does not double running speed. Attribute curves and training gains are unchanged; their relative match value still needs controlled measurement.'), '25': ('Corrected; no game change', 'The proposed repeated-animation shortcut already exists. Cross-player setup is ordinary management. The report now states this throughout.'), '26': ('Your choice', 'Temporary training penalties encouraged banking TP. Choice: keep delayed spending as valid strategy, or replace those penalties with a different tradeoff.'), '27': ('Your choice', 'Some reserve requests had little practical cost. Choice: keep occasional easy kindness decisions, or make their costs depend more on squad use.'), '28': ('Unproven economy claim', 'Late cash grew, but I did not exhaust useful existing upgrades. There is no established need for a new money sink. Compare existing spending options before changing income or wages.'), '29': ('Your choice', 'Power presentations sometimes replace the coaching dock while the match advances. Choice: keep that cinematic layout, or reserve space for coaching controls during powers.'), '30': ('Fixed locally', 'README, project context, the power rules, and the playtest handoff now describe bought permits, automatic licensing, the season-one exception, promise blocks, and the Tier 4/Tier 5 efficiency exception.')}
for item in issues:
 item["status"], item["resolution"] = fix_status[item["id"]]
assert len(issues)==30
